# Node dependencies, any depth. No .gitignore at repo root existed before
# this, so nothing stopped a `git add -A` from picking up node_modules in a
# sibling top-level dir (e.g. marketing-site/) that isn't under dataops-agent/,
# whose own .gitignore only covers itself and below.
node_modules/

# Database dumps. These must never enter version control: they are multi-MB,
# they hold real tenant data, and at least one of them
# (dataops_backup_pre_encryption_20260830.sql) predates Item #1's credential
# encryption migration, so it contains data-source passwords as PLAINTEXT JSON
# — committing it would put those in git history permanently, where removing
# them later means a history rewrite rather than a delete.
#
# Until now this directory was merely untracked, not ignored, so a single
# `git add -A` would have swept all three dumps in. Keep the backups themselves
# somewhere durable outside git (external drive / cloud storage).
backups/
